C:\Users\wilso\Documents\APPS\origen_app_erp\ORIGEN\components\auth\LoginForm.tsx:
  Line 159:                 aria-label={showPassword ? 'Ocultar contraseña' : 'Mostrar contraseña'}

The "Mostrar" label wraps the select, so `getByLabel('Mostrar')` resolves to the select. `selectOption('archived')` works (value='archived').

So after archiving and switching to 'archived', the code should have count 0 because the filter shows only ARCHIVED projects and the project was archived → it SHOULD be visible!

Wait, the test:
```js
await page.getByRole('button', { name: `Archivar proyecto ${projectData.code}` }).click();
await page.getByLabel('Mostrar').selectOption('archived');
await page.waitForTimeout(2000);
await expect(page.getByText(projectData.code)).toHaveCount(0);
```

That's backwards! After archiving, switching the filter to "Archivados" SHOWS the archived project. The expectation `toHaveCount(0)` is wrong.

Looking at `ui-ux` UI-008:
```js
